Europass layout theme
---------------------
The europass theme is drawn after the layout of the Europass CV template (Word, 2013-2019),
© European Union, 2002-2015, published by Cedefop at https://europass.cedefop.europa.eu.
Content owned by the European Union is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International licence (CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), as the
European Union's legal notice states (https://european-union.europa.eu/legal-notice_en):
reuse is allowed, provided appropriate credit is given and changes are indicated.

Source: the Europass CV template, © European Union, 2002-2015 | europass.cedefop.europa.eu.
Licence: CC BY 4.0.
Changes: the layout was redrawn from scratch as HTML and CSS templates for Postulo, set in
Arimo instead of Arial, with contact icons drawn for this plugin, a portfolio and a letter
the original does not have, right-to-left support, and without the language grid, the "Job
applied for" row, the logo and the footer. No file, text or image of the template is
included; the words the theme prints are in this plugin's own catalogues.

Not covered, and not used: the legal notice excludes logos and names from the licence
("logos and names ... are excluded from the Commission's reuse policy and are not licensed
to you"). The plugin ships no Europass or European Union logo, emblem or flag. The word
"Europass" appears only to say which layout the theme follows ("Europass layout").

This plugin is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by Europass, Cedefop or the
European Commission. The europass theme is inspired by the Europass CV and is not the
Europass CV.
